Strict Windows decoding accepts the C1 fills of undefined bytes
(CP1252 0x81 is U+0081) and the EUDC pairs; it rejects every
undefined byte that the lenient decode sends to the private-use
area, every invalid trail byte, and a lead byte at the end or
before NUL.
.B glyphs
is a decode token; encoding a glyph character back to its byte is
Windows' best fit, which writes U+263A as 0x01.
.H 3 "Premap Tokens"
.P
A premap is one character-level map applied between decoding and
encoding.
At most one is given per call.
It applies in the domain of the call: on bytes between transfer
encodings
.RB ( raw
to
.BR raw ),
on code points between charsets.
