.H 3 "Compile-Time Errors"
.P
Every misuse of
.B convert()
is a compile-time error that names the offending argument, and no
argument is replaced by a default.
A token that cannot apply to the pair is an error, never ignored.
Two kinds of token that apply but cannot change the result are
dropped, so the instruction is the same as without them:
.B fail
where the tokens in force, given or default, leave nothing
unmappable, and an ill-formed-source
token on a source that defines every byte (Section 4.3.1).
The messages are:
