.TB "Windows Case Table (compare Section 4.6)"
.P
.B LCMapStringEx
with
.B LCMAP_LINGUISTIC_CASING
gives the plain simple mapping on the first five of these
characters, with no final-sigma rule, as
.B ulower()
and
.B uupper()
do.
Like the standard table, it leaves the Cherokee and Georgian
letters unmapped, where
.B ulower()
and
.B uupper()
map them (Section 4.6.1).
.H 3 "LM Password Preparation"
.P
Windows prepares an LM password with
.BR RtlUpcaseUnicodeStringToOemString :
uppercase, then convert to the OEM code page.
Measured on Windows 11, that is not \(lquppercase, then encode\(rq
by any rule.
Best fit applies (U+0101 becomes
.BR A ),
and
\(lq\[u0131]\(rq, which
.B RtlUpcaseUnicodeChar
leaves unchanged and CP437 best-fits to
.BR i ,
becomes
.BR I .
The closest closed-form rule found still misses 14 of the 65,536
BMP code points for CP437.
The
.B upper_oem
premap is therefore a direct table from code point to OEM byte,
dumped per OEM page by running Windows' uppercase-to-OEM
conversion
.RB ( RtlUpcaseUnicodeToCustomCPN
over each page's table) on every BMP code point; for CP437 the
dump equals the system's own OEM path on all 65,536.
