default character (0x3F, or 0x6F on the EBCDIC pages) and is not
itself the character that byte decodes to.
A character that best-fits to
.B ?
is therefore unmappable, and under
.B fail
gives a null result.
Measured on Windows 11:
.B RtlUpcaseUnicodeStringToOemString
fails on U+FF1F (fullwidth question mark) and U+2047 (double
question mark), and
.B WideCharToMultiByte
reports that it used the default character for both, while
.B ?
and \(lq\[u00BF]\(rq convert normally.
hx gives the same four results.
